9e5e3ad4|4|10 months ago|3|1|H|Nice product|⭐ Review: realme Buds T200x I recently purchased the realme Buds T200x, and after using it for a while, here is my honest and professional review: --- ✅ What I Like The 12.4mm dynamic bass drivers deliver deep and powerful bass. Music sounds punchy and lively, especially for EDM, Bollywood, and hip-hop. The ANC (Active Noise Cancellation) works well for low-to-medium background noise such as fan noise or traffic hum. It does not block everything, but considering the price, it performs well. The battery backup is impressive. With the charging case, it easily lasts long enough for daily usage without frequent charging. The earbuds are very lightweight and comfortable, making them suitable for long listening sessions. The touch gesture controls for music play/pause, next/previous track, volume, and mode switching work smoothly without delay. --- ⚠ Missing Feature / Limitation While the touch gestures work well for music and media control, there is no dedicated touch gesture to answer or reject phone calls. The call control feature must be done through the phone, which can be slightly inconvenient, especially when the phone is in a pocket or bag. --- 🎯 Final Verdict Overall, the realme Buds T200x offers great value for money with strong bass, reliable ANC, long battery life, and smooth touch controls for music. If Realme added touch control for phone calls, it would have been nearly perfect for this price segment. Still, considering performance, comfort, and features, it is a solid and worth-buying product in its budget range. Thanks Realme-hope future upgrade includes call control gesture.
