52a44445|5|Dec, 2023|1|1|H|Best in the market!|These TWS earphones are great for the price offered. The vocals are clear, bass is not overpowering and only as much required and good instrument separation. Also, the different modes that are available in HeyMelody app are considerably recognisable. The battery backup is great, too. A full charge gets these beauties going for 3-4 days at 50% volume and 6-8 hours of usage. The texture of the TWD is slippery though, and should have been grippy for comfortable handling. Call quality is phenomenal too, thanks to the quad mic setup. I have been using them for a few months and they function as new. Overall, it's value for money and provides premium performance in the budget range.
086e033f|5|Dec, 2023|1|1|H|Just wow!|This product is an absolute value for money. Now let me explain why. Sound quality:- this thing sounds so good that I cannot explain. Like the stereo surround sound effect with Dolby Atmos is just fantastic. The vocals, the highs, the lows, and the last but not least is the bass. The bass is seriously crazy! It's not gonna feel heavy but the balance of it with every other instrument is just phenomenal. I'm not saying that the bass is less or that it's balanced. Its high enough to fit perfectly with other sounds. Connectivity:- it's pretty good. No issues in that. You might face some delay of sound rarely when you start while watching Netflix or something but it will be back to normal if you wait for a sec or just repair it. Build quality:- Not good really. It's average. I said that because the hinge of the case is slightly loose and it Wiggles sometimes. Buds are good and no issues in their build quality. Mic quality: it works great and the noise cancellation works pretty good whether you are outside or inside. I had no issues. It sounds fine.
