036aab21|4|Apr, 2024|40|1|H|Good quality product|Let's start with the good thing first: the sound quality. It's an 8/10. In the original sound quality mode the bass is almost unavailable in most songs. So if you like to hear good bass as well, you have to change the mode to bass mode. Then it produces really good bass, but the rest of the sound becomes a little off in bass mode. So, I normally use the original mode with a 3rd party equalizer bass turned on. There is one other mode called voice mode or something which I never used. The battery isn't bad or good. It can run for a maximum of 3 to 4 hours, and the case can charge the headphones 5 to 6 times. Now, let's get to the bad parts, and there are a lot: 1. There is no Dolby Atmos in these headphones, which is a complete lie. 2. The touch areas are really really small. You have to try two or three times to make it work because it's so small. 3. There is no AI noise cancellation at all. In fact, I think it's made to capture more noises. 4. The design of these headphones is terrible, especially the case, It's completely round which makes it really hard to find the opening of the case, especially at night. The headphones make my ears hurt if I use them for longer than two hours, which didn't happen with my previous headphones. 5. When I use them with my laptop, sometimes they lower the sound quality for half a second and then get back to normal immediately. It's very annoying. It doesn't happen with my phone though. And It also didn't happen with my previous headphones. 6. After using them with my laptop, if I connect them to my phone, I have to manually connect them via Bluetooth. The same thing happens when I switch from phone to laptop after using them.
