42fd8ba9|4|Apr, 2018|7|1|H|Worth the money|I have been using Logitech wireless Computer assesary for quite a while now,and I have to say it just keeps getting better and better. I bought the mouse to recollaborate the familiar desktop feel we all grew up with and wireless usability gave it just the notch it needed to acquire the modern status,after all everything in techo-realm is heading towards the wireless,but seemless experience. So we'll see about the product now:- 1)It is everything it promises to be and more. 2)The synchronisation between the gesture speed and actual hardware is satisfactory. 3)radius is quite good on this product as it gives us ability to work from all the distance we can think of while keeping our sights on the the monitor. 4)Huge battery backup is as promising as it's told in the manual,it gives us quite few weeks on heavy usage. 5)For all who have used a similar product before will know how big of a frustration it is to lose your connector,well they have a solution for you. The main mouse hardware itself contains a slot to keep your connector safe while moving the setup around. Personally my experience was great with the assessary and I'll highly recommend you to spend a few bucks more and get a much more reliable product from a top order company in this field for years. I hope you find my efforts useful.
